## Context

Reading-3 (tracker [[0605]]). Figures 6 (`fig:exp2-arms`, coverage) and 7
(`fig:exp2-arms-cost`, cost) are unreadable at column width — fonts too
small. Both are produced by `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py`
(panels coverage + cost), included at `\linewidth`.

Current font sizes are small (`plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py`): bar value
labels `fontsize=6.0` (`:334`), x-tick labels `7.5` (`:342`), y-ticks
`7.5` (`:346`), axis title `9` (`:345`), condition legend `8.5` (`:389`),
in-plot annotations `8` (`:263`, `:276`), suptitle `13` (`:388`).

## Actions

1. Increase the font sizes so the figures are legible at one-column width
   (the 6.0 / 7.5 / 8 / 8.5 / 9 values are the offenders — bump
   proportionally; the 6.0 bar labels especially). Prefer setting a
   sensible base via `rcParams`/a single scale factor over hand-tuning
   each call, so both panels stay consistent.
2. Keep the layout from overflowing — if larger fonts crowd the bars,
   adjust figure size / spacing so nothing clips. Verify against the
   rendered PDF at `\linewidth`.
3. Regenerate `fig_exp2_arms_coverage.pdf` and `fig_exp2_arms_cost.pdf`
   via the `render.mk` target; commit both.

## Coordination

- [[0622]] (Wikipedia line) and [[0623]] (Figure 6 caption) touch the same
  figure/emitter — sequence/stack to avoid emitter conflicts; the
  GEM→Wikipedia annotation text (`:263`) is also a font/label site.

## Relevant files

- `src/aedist/plot_exp2_arms_comparison.py` — all the `fontsize=`/
  `labelsize=` sites above.
- `report/inputs/generated/fig_exp2_arms_coverage.pdf`,
  `fig_exp2_arms_cost.pdf` (regenerate).

## Test

- Red first: a unit/adherence check that the emitter's base font size is
  ≥ a legible threshold (e.g. no `fontsize` below N in the script), so the
  regression (tiny fonts) cannot silently return.

